Z||000019||87GTBro||02-20-2000||09:21 PM||||Shiner,<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> I get really bad gas mileage on my 86 V6 as well.  I calculated about 12mpg.  I drive around the city and have to fill up again.  And that is not fun with the gas prices sky-rocketing.<P>I attributed the bad gas mileage to leaking fuel injectors because sometimes when the engine is warm (has been recently driven) and I try to start it again, the engine is flooded.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  It takes quite a while to get it started.<P>I bought some Berryman's B-12 Complete Fuel System Treatment and put it in my gas tank and filled her up today and so-far I haven't had any problems.  <P>You should try it.  Only cost $7.  That's better than $370 for new injectors.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87GTBro (edited 02-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||Greg Piet||02-21-2000||02:27 AM||||If you need to push he pedal to the metal to start it, you are starting the car in "flood" mode"  as far as the computer is concerned.  Ths problem may be a  defective cold start injector which is convenietly tucked behind the distributor.  I have no idea how often thes things go, but there is a section on this in my 85 service manual.||||reg||1
